# Copy to .env.production in the approved stable worktree only.
NEXORA_ENV=production
# Defaults: API 127.0.0.1:8100, Web 127.0.0.1:3100
# Runtime defaults to <this worktree>/.runtime/production
# Optional absolute overrides; every writable path must be under NEXORA_RUNTIME_ROOT:
# NEXORA_RUNTIME_ROOT=
# NEXORA_JOURNAL_PATH=
# NEXORA_STATE_PATH=
# NEXORA_CHECKPOINT_PATH=
# Research recovery checkpoints (ADR-022) live in the checkpoint path above;
# on by default. "off" forces full journal replay on every start.
# NEXORA_RESEARCH_CHECKPOINTS=on
# NEXORA_LOG_PATH=
# NEXORA_CACHE_PATH=
# Copy approved research JSON unchanged into this stable worktree before configuring:
# NEXORA_RESEARCH_CONFIG=
# ADR-023/024: keep unset until validation and human approval of a PROD change.
# Unset means all optional features DISABLED. No runtime switch or trading authority.
# NEXORA_FEATURES_CONFIG=
# NEXORA_BACKTEST_CONFIG_DIR=
# Optional read-only MT5 source. Preserve the verified existing offset/configuration.
# NEXORA_MT5_PATH=
# NEXORA_MT5_SYMBOL=
# NEXORA_MT5_TIME_OFFSET_SECONDS=0
# PostgreSQL credentials must be supplied locally; separate DB/role + identity required.
# NEXORA_POSTGRES_DSN=
# Secure remote access (REMOTE1): the exact public HTTPS origin exposed through the
# tunnel (e.g. https://nexora.example.com, or a Tailscale Serve MagicDNS hostname
# such as https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net). Not a secret; still opt-in and unset
# by default - remote access stays off until this is set. See
# tasks/REMOTE1-secure-remote-access.md.
#
# For a Tailscale Serve deployment this is the ONLY variable required for remote
# access. There is no per-device IP to configure: a remote request is trusted at
# the transport layer only when it carries a non-empty Tailscale-User-Login header
# (Tailscale Serve's own WhoIs-authenticated identity, empirically verified to be
# stripped-then-regenerated by Serve itself - a client cannot forge it), AND its
# Origin matches this exact value, independently. Any device already permitted on
# your tailnet works automatically; there is no NEXORA_LOCAL_TAILSCALE_IP or
# similar per-device setting - an earlier peer-IP-based design (PR #26) was tried
# and disproved by real-device testing; do not reintroduce it.
# NEXORA_EXTERNAL_ORIGIN=
